<title>THAILAND: Siam Commercial group to underwrite bond.</title>
<headline>Siam Commercial group to underwrite bond.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Thailand's Siam Commercial Bank Plc won a bid to underwrite the state Provincial Waterworks Authority's seven-year bonds worth 800 million baht ($30.7 million), a finance ministry official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The group was awarded the bid by offering the lowest interest rate of 10.30 percent per annum, the official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The consortium includes Thai Summit Finance and Securities Co Ltd, Bangkok Metropolitan Bank Plc and Bank of Ayudhya Plc, he said.</p>
<p>The state agency will use proceeds from the issue to expand its water distribution network in the provinces, he added.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
